The Runnable interface is a functional interface because it has only one abstract method (run()). This makes it a perfect candidate for Java 8's lambda expressions, which provide a highly concise syntax.
This is not a new way of creating threads, but rather a modern, compact syntax for creating a Runnable instance on the fly.

